{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages","id":1429497,"title":"Anime Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-22T06:35:47-08:00","id":1429497,"title":"Anime Mages","content":"So, I've been on a bit of a Yu Yu Hakusho kick for a week now. And it occured to me that their magic system is actually consistent enough to maybe form the basis of a character in mage.<br /> <br /> Then it occured to me, how would you use spheres to reproduce the typical fight tropes of a shonen anime?<br /> <br /> Life 2 healing to have an attack have 'missed any vital spots.' with it becoming more vulgar the more obviously vital the hit was?<br /> <br /> Forces 3 for anime leaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T11:40:17-08:00","id":1429537,"title":"","content":"Break out the Akashic Brotherhood Tradition Book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T11:43:33-08:00","id":1429538,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Brotherhood is the way to go for that kind of Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T11:44:09-08:00","id":1429539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429537#post1429537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Break out the Akashic Brotherhood Tradition Book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragons of the east in general","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T11:57:25-08:00","id":1429542,"title":"","content":"While, with good reason, people get a bit meh on it, M20's How Do You Do That does have a whole chapter that's relevant to this.<br /> <br /> Though unless you're planning on running a game in the Umbra (which is fair if you're talking YYH) Vulgar is going to pretty quickly kick most shonen tropes off the table. More martial arts focused titles like Fist of the North Star or Baki the Grappler are going to be much easier shonen stories to practically accomplish with Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-22T12:55:16-08:00","id":1429549,"title":"","content":"In Naruto, summoning of spirit animals is basically something Marauders do (they call it &quot;Zooterrorism&quot; in some of the books.) You use Spirit to summon a spirit powerful enough to use the Materialize charm across the Gauntlet (which, I think, would be coincidental, since the &quot;True Magick&quot; part is the summoning--the overt part is accomplished via the Spirit's own static powers.) Similarly, being Jinchuriki, is just Spirit 4, and finding a spirit with a lot of power and the right charms (though, since we're talking about Shonen here, &quot;Blast&quot; is probably nonnegotiable lol.) The interesting thing there is that Spirit 4 covers both methods for creating a Jinchuriki (i.e., subjugation, or making nice-nice.)<br /> <br /> Obviously this is very Naruto-specific, but Naruto is far from the only shonen in which people summon fantastical creatures to fight on their behalf, or use/absorb their power.<br /> <br /> Another fun one is that the &quot;Caster Gun&quot; from <i>Outlaw Star </i>is big gun that activates cylindrical Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T06:19:36-08:00","id":1429617,"title":"","content":"Getting a powerful spirit patron to either eat paradox or simply prevent people from perceiving anything paradoxical ( an area effect version of the Blatancy skill? ). You'd need a pact of some kind and rules covering honorable use of the patronage.<br /> <br /> The rules required could help encourage acting like Anime characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T09:47:16-08:00","id":1429636,"title":"","content":"Even with Allies 5, Avatar 5, Blessing 5, Familiar 5, Legend 5, Totem 5 and I guess swiping the Possessed rules from WtA and allowing mages to be possessed without it interfering with being mages... you're not actually going to be a running around Paradox free as you pull off ninjustu like Naruto does or some such.<br /> <br /> Sure, all of that is going to make for a very powerful mage that can do a lot of stuff, but that's in the context of Mage, not in the context of shonen manga/anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T15:25:02-08:00","id":1429683,"title":"","content":"I thought the Akashic Brotherhood was the anime tradition?<br /> <br /> Plus how would you use a stand/persona?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T16:13:33-08:00","id":1429689,"title":"","content":"The Akashics are the &quot;Physical discipline is Magic,&quot; Tradition, which covers some common anime stuff, and lots of other stuff, just as anime - even shonen anime - is a hell of a lot broader.<br /> <br /> Though if you wanted something close to a Stand? Manifest Avatar attached to a Familiar built with M20 Gods &amp; Monsters has the basic mechanics. Even if, again, you're not getting anything as bizarre as the source inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T17:10:57-08:00","id":1429693,"title":"","content":"The big point is that Anime doesn't push a Subtle world. There is no masquerade/Rule of shade/Veil for some reason in a world where demons blatantly exist and psychic detectives can blast you iwth their finger people don't believe in the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Now the Nasuverse(Fate series, Meltyblood, etc) does have Rule of Shade/Veil/Masquerade and does cover how these over the top battles could exist in a world that looks generally like ours without people knowing the way of wizards and Vampires. Alot of stuff happens in parallel reality zones, or extra dimensions(the equivalent of the umbra). I would imagine it would be relatively easy to replicate much fo the spells in the series and have had Servants show up in games in the past.(They are summoned High Umbral spirits... some more powerful than others... Don't summon Gilgamesh)<br /> <br /> The various metaphysics of the Persona games also might be a good source for a Paradigm and Practice...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T18:46:39-08:00","id":1429700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429542#post1429542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More martial arts focused titles like Fist of the North Star or Baki the Grappler are going to be much easier shonen stories to practically accomplish with Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to find a way to watch the original Baki series somehow. I've only seen the recent Netflix sequel, which is pretty good, although I could tell by about episode 3 or so that I was clearly missing a lot of backstory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429689#post1429689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Akashics are the &quot;Physical discipline is Magic,&quot; Tradition, which covers some common anime stuff, and lots of other stuff, just as anime - even shonen anime - is a hell of a lot broader.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're more the &quot;reality is an illusion, and once you see past it, physical limitations no longer matter&quot; tradition.<br /> The Euthanatoi, Celestial Chorus, Dreamspeakers and certain Hermetics also get into the whole &quot;superhuman warrior&quot; schtick to some degree. (Wu Lung, Batini, and Templars as well.) There's a place for that in the Verbena and Etherites also, IMO at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 12-23-2020, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T19:10:25-08:00","id":1429701,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429693#post1429693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big point is that Anime doesn't push a Subtle world. There is no masquerade/Rule of shade/Veil for some reason in a world where demons blatantly exist and psychic detectives can blast you iwth their finger people don't believe in the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Jujutsu Kaisen is about the only thing I've seen recently that has any degree of &quot;masquerade&quot; going on. <br /> <br /> As opposed to, say, God of High School, which started as a high school sports tournament and escalated very quickly. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T20:17:26-08:00","id":1429707,"title":"","content":"The God of High School has the kind of masquerade the Traditions wish they had. Simply put, in a world where this is <i>not</i> magic:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media1.tenor.com/images/ab2a88002321a3f68c86573c386f165b/tenor.gif?itemid=18312090\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Who\u2019s ever going to suspect that this <i>is</i>:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/-se9hWP_EP4/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T20:35:30-08:00","id":1429709,"title":"","content":"I think that's really missing the point. the WOD broadly promotes a &quot;The world looks like ours&quot; with some differences but most of the crazy shit being shifted off into other realms. I think that would be how one would have to integrate a more &quot;anime&quot; situation. Stands would go back to being metaphors for psychic fights. Battles with spirits require trips to the spirit plane though failing to stop them might cause unexplained fires.. that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T21:12:45-08:00","id":1429710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429707#post1429707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God of High School has the kind of masquerade the Traditions wish they had. Simply put, in a world where this is <i>not</i> magic:</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I am aware, it is a world where certain people have power from either directly channeling the power of gods and other divine archetypes or are able to wield the power of divine weapons. The only real exceptions to this are one character who is apparently the single most bad ass normal human being on the planet, and his grandson, who is an even more unique case.<br /> <br /> But the masses of people watching the fights largely seem to accept the manifestation of divine power as totally normal. Though this may be some sort of commentary by the creator about Korean/Asian worldviews vs those of Westerners; I can't really tell. (The American government seems seriously alarmed by events.)<br /> <br /> I suppose in Mage, it is entirely possible that an over the top anime style battle might result in some sort of Paradox backlash that seals the fight of from mundane reality. Alternately, a Mauder who believes they are a shonen battle anime character may have some sort of reality bubble around them which sucks everyone in it into the delusion until the Marauder goes elsewhere , at which point they remember damage and destruction as the result of some sort of disaster or othe event.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T23:53:24-08:00","id":1429719,"title":"","content":"A lot of urban fantasy anime do something to the extent of, &quot;normal humans can't see the supernatural for what it really is and try to rationalize whatever impact they do see as best they can.&quot;<br /> <br /> My point though, was that &quot;anime&quot; is a lot bigger than big flashy supernatural fights. Shonen is bigger than that. Gundam is a shonen anime franchise and it'd be even harder to pull off in Mage besides taking it to the Umbra because Paradox would wreck mecha way harder than it would smack you for tossing a few ki blasts at someone. Sword Art Online is a shonen anime, and basically doesn't require any sort of adjustment to do in Mage because that's just bog standard VA/ME stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-24T17:12:01-08:00","id":1429795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429693#post1429693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The various metaphysics of the Persona games also might be a good source for a Paradigm and Practice...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually there is a Craft introduced in M20 that is basically the SMT/Persona Craft, the Mirainohmen. Sadly they only got a couple sentences in the section discussing future potential members of the Disparate Alliance. As a fan of SMT/Persona, I really would have loved to see how they would have tackled such a group though with the current state of things I doubt we'll seem them anytime soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T13:12:26-08:00","id":1429890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1429497-anime-mages?p=1429710#post1429710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I am aware, it is a world where certain people have power from either directly channeling the power of gods and other divine archetypes or are able to wield the power of divine weapons. The only real exceptions to this are one character who is apparently the single most bad ass normal human being on the planet, and his grandson, who is an even more unique case.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the narrative contrivance of every serious martial artist outside of the Seoul regional tournament <i>having</i> borrowed power muddies the waters some, it\u2019s explicitly explained to be the secret \u201creal magic\u201d in a world that otherwise runs on standard martial arts mysticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}